Bug summary: SimplexSolver (Apache Commons Math) throws UnboundedSolutionException on feasible, bounded minimization LPs (DEA-style problems with randomly generated data), and the number of failures grows with the number of variables. Matlab solves the same problems without unbounded results. This points to a pivoting/ratio-test bug, probably in how near-zero or degenerate pivot entries are handled.

